    "result_text": "The repository contains a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`, with `AcceptanceBase` as its abstract support), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the possible-duplicate soft-match rule for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** when a new owner isn't a hard (identity-key) duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` while carrying a *different* telephone, the owner is still created and comes back with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (lowest id if several match). Otherwise `possibleDuplicate` is `false` and `possibleDuplicateOf` is absent.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added persistent `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) fields with accessors and `toString`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n- `service/ClinicService(+Impl).java` \u2014 new `findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId(Owner)` that finds a matching owner by normalized last name + postcode + differing telephone, deterministically returning the lowest id.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the hard-duplicate check passes, computes and sets the two flags before save.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `possibleDuplicate` (coalescing null\u2192false), lets `possibleDuplicateOf` map by name, and ignores both on the write-side `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping.\n\nBuild compiles cleanly and `AcceptanceTest` passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
