    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and closely follows the conventions already established in this codebase.\n\n- **Field + persistence plumbing** (`Owner.java`, four `schema.sql` dialects, `openapi.yml`) mirror the existing `bulkSignupWarning` feature field-for-field: column, getter/setter pair, `toString` append, schema column with the same ordering/defaults, and a `readOnly` OpenAPI property with a clear description. Nothing is duplicated or misplaced.\n\n- **Matching logic lives in the service layer** (`findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId` in `ClinicServiceImpl`), which is the right unit. It's structurally parallel to the neighbouring `isIdentityKeyInUse` \u2014 same `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()` approach, same reuse of the shared `normalizeForComparison` helper \u2014 and the interface Javadoc explicitly contrasts the two, which a maintainer would find natural.\n\n- **The controller stays thin**: it calls the service and sets the two derived fields, exactly matching the adjacent `owner.setNamesakeCount(this.clinicService.countNamesakes(...))` pattern. Orchestration here is consistent with how the create path already assembles derived fields.\n\n- **Mapper** adds `formatPossibleDuplicate` in the same `default`-method style as `formatBulkSignupWarning`/`formatContactPreference`, and correctly marks both new fields `ignore` on the request\u2192entity mapping alongside the other server-derived fields. Letting `possibleDuplicateOf` map by name (no custom formatter needed) is appropriate since it's a passthrough integer.\n\nNo class or method is turning into a catch-all, and the responsibilities are split along the existing controller/service/mapper/model seams.",
